WEBVTT

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.480
There are a total of five Phi-Brain children

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.820
with the potential to serve as my vessel.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.840
Gammon Sakanoue,

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.420
Freecell,

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:22.290
and Raetsel is drawing ever
closer to an acceptable level.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.600
There is also Kaito Daimon.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.470
His actions have gone so far as
to sway the future I foresaw.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.840
He is a truly fascinating individual.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.470
You are my problem child,
Rook Banjo Crossfield.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.860
You are the most skilled after Kaito,

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.590
and yet you completely reject the
idea of becoming a Phi-Brain.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.580
No one can escape me,
regardless of who he might be.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:30.000
Kaito, You’ve Lost

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.810
Bishop, have any reports come in
from the Orpheus Order?

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.510
No, nothing yet.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.010
But knowing them,
I’m confident they will find something.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.170
They have worshipped Orpheus
since ancient times,

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.480
so the chances that they will provide us
with information are extremely good.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.500
It was most astute of you to
think of them, Master Rook.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.360
Please continue the investigation.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.490
Most certainly.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.590
I was able to see the future.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.330
This is the one and only way to
defeat Orpheus... and save Jin.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:17.590
This is what I must do.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:22.380
Jin?!

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.010
No, Orpheus!

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:30.210
Rook Banjo Crossfield,
aren’t you using the Orpheus Order

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.400
to search for a way to defeat me?

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.150
I’ve already told you.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.960
I can easily see such blatant maneuvers.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.130
Bastard!

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.290
It’s no use.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.030
You cannot escape the future
I have already witnessed.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.620
I shall enlighten you.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.300
Here is what you are truly meant to do...

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:10.560
Yummy cake! The Pre-Pre rocks!

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.940
It’s the Pretty Melancholy!

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:17.080
Remember this isn’t your house!

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:21.190
<i>I want to eat cake. I want to eat cake.</i>

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.130
I didn’t realize Director Rook had
asked that of the Orpheus Order...

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.950
It worked out perfectly.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.280
<i>Please give some cake to me as well.</i>

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.170
I had been searching for a way to assist

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.200
Freecell in whatever way I could.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.440
<i>Me, too! Me, too!</i>

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.720
Sheesh! Even I’m stuck helping!

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:34.740
It’s made this past week
an absolute nightmare!

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.740
<i>Give cake to me as well.</i>

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.420
So what did you guys learn about Orpheus?

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:42.920
Would you be so kind as
to ask them in person?

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.440
<i>“Them” who?</i>

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.540
I can’t spend forever on this!

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:55.690
Damn it!

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.370
Kaito?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:00.070
I don’t have time for this crap!

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.710
Th-that’s not true! Right, Freecell?

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.920
Freecell Yeah. Kaito, you and I have

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.830
definitely improved since
we started the Trial of--

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.620
That’s not what I’m talking about!

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.550
I want to face Orpheus.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.020
I’ve gotta defeat him as soon as
I possibly can and save Jin!

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:26.190
But when the heck will I get
to duel him in a puzzle?

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:32.860
Rook?

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.500
Yo! I brought them.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.260
Doubt! Mizerka!

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:04.840
Rook...

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:10.820
Isn’t this a beautiful city?

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:16.320
It looks just like a puzzle made by the gods.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.000
Dude, what brings you to Amgine?

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:25.710
When I thought of you, I
couldn’t help but come.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.540
So how is it coming along with Jin?

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.600
I’m not getting anywhere.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.970
I can’t even get near Orpheus.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:39.010
And here I’ve gotta hurry and rescue Jin!

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.720
Then you’ll have to keep at it.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.050
Rook!

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:03.790
What is this?!

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.210
A puzzle that I made.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.030
Rook?!

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.310
I built it so you and I could battle.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:15.030
What?!

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.560
We’ll ride our individual coasters
as we head toward the goal.

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:33.570
Whichever side gets through the maze
and reaches the goal first wins.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:38.820
However, this maze has three sets of
gates planted on both tracks.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:43.080
If one of us passes through a gate,
its corresponding gate will close.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.870
Whoever is trailing behind
will crash into the wall.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.780
Game over!

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.520
Say what?!

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:54.130
There are some other rules,

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:58.260
but you’re capable of figuring them
out as out as we go, aren’t you?

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.790
Hey, Rook!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:02.410
Kaito, you can’t bow out.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.670
Puzzle time... Let’s begin!

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:16.800
Cut the crap! What the
hell are you thinking?!

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:21.430
There is only one way to save Jin.
I’ll let you know what it is.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:28.340
I must become Orpheus’
vessel and replace Jin,

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.440
allowing his mind to enter mine.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:34.250
You shouldn’t be so surprised.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.490
I imagine my mind will cease to
exist when that happens.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:40.470
But that is a trivial matter.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:43.150
After all, in doing that,

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.390
I’ll be able to make
Orpheus’ dream become reality!

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:50.460
His dream? What are you talking--

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.600
Rook, you didn’t!

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.280
Yes, I did!

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:05.370
Orpheus bequeathed another Armlet unto me!

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.620
Orpheus did?!

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.530
I’ve made my mind.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.560
I will sacrifice myself for Orpheus’ ideal.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.670
I will solve the Puzzle of
God and become a Phi-Brain!

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:22.370
Master Rook!

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.470
Just as I feared, Master
Rook has donned the Armlet!

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:29.310
Exactly!

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.390
Enigma, you bastard!

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:38.230
At the moment, Rook is consumed
with his loyalty to Orpheus

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:41.640
and the desire to become a Phi-Brain.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.200
A larger audience is always desirable.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.450
Why don’t we watch the spectacle together?

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.950
Let’s see how this battle ends.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:54.540
Please... save Master Rook!

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.780
Kaito, I know exactly what you have in mind.

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:04.130
I won’t let you lay so
much as a finger on Orpheus.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:08.790
I will make sure that his
ideal is made a reality!

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:11.640
Has the Armlet consumed him...?

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.090
Rook, come to your senses!

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.980
You’re mistaken. I have come to my senses.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:23.600
I owe it to the power of this Armlet
that Orpheus gave me!

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:27.910
What should I do? At this rate...

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:32.110
At any rate, the two of us have to
get outta this puzzle alive!

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:38.000
I swear I’ll break that Armlet again
and bring back the old you!

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.860
Are you up to the task, Kaito?

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:45.370
Is that it? Is that my first gate?

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:50.690
If I pass through it first, Rook will die.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.660
If Rook’s first, I’ll die.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.940
So the only way both of
us will make it out alive

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:59.110
is if I make sure we’re
synchronized all three times!

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:04.390
I’m up to the challenge! Bring it on!

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:09.570
The coaster’s speed is set on auto,
so I can’t control it.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.790
I can change routes at the track
switches when I need to.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:20.030
I can’t control the red track switches.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:24.780
It’s set to automatically switch
once a coaster passes through.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.470
All right! This is where
I’ve gotta tweak my timing!

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:37.190
He passed through.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.060
Go!

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:50.600
Sweet!

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.990
Simultaneous entry? You’re soft, Kaito!

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:55.730
What?

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:59.230
Sure enough, you aren’t worthy
to serve as Orpheus’ vessel

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.540
if you lack what it takes
to defeat your rivals!

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.690
There is only one who
can realize his ideal...

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.490
and that is me!

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:09.240
Orpheus!

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:15.000
Tell me, Rook! What the
hell is Orpheus’ ideal?!

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:17.250
Are you curious?

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:30.460
It’s hard to believe, but
apparently it’s all true.

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:36.020
I can’t believe the Orpheus
we worshipped still exists.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.830
And to think he’s trying to execute
such a terrifying plan!

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:42.030
What’s that?

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:45.630
Everything was recorded in
this ancient manuscript.

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:52.470
It claims that Orpheus’ dream is to confront
the Ultimate Giver and surpass Him.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.260
The Ultimate Giver?

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:55.840
God.

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.440
This is a massive puzzle
that has been going on

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.300
between Orpheus and the gods for thousands of years.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:09.540
Orpheus has two Phi-Brain children fight.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:12.640
Then he claims the winner as his
new vessel for his mind.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.170
He has gained that ability through
playing these puzzles with the gods.

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:19.620
By casting aside his body,

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:23.570
he has conquered the yoke called “death,”
which the gods placed on us.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.800
However, that was merely a checkpoint.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:32.090
When he is free of the greatest
yoke, known as “time,”

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:35.080
Orpheus will surpass the gods.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:38.060
This manuscript made it blatantly clear.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:41.930
The moment he manages to
solve all of the gods’ puzzles,

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:46.090
Orpheus will be the only person
left standing on Earth.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:57.120
Mankind will surpass the gods!

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.980
Don’t you think that is a wonderful dream?

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.480
So what about his puzzles with the gods?!

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:07.780
If solving them means Orpheus is
the only one who will survive...

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.660
that isn’t a dream or an ideal!

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:14.090
Really! Jin is such an idiot.

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:16.640
If he had humbly submitted
to Orpheus and vanished,

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:21.420
he would have been able to
achieve his goal by now!

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.630
Rook, you bastard!

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:29.430
Jin sacrificed his memories
to seal Orpheus within his own body!

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.430
You dare call that stupid?!

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.360
You’re equally stupid, Kaito.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.240
Kaito, if you didn’t
recover Jin’s memories,

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:42.750
Orpheus would still be
sound asleep inside of him.

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:49.070
Thank you for waking Orpheus back up, Kaito.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.620
You’re right. I’m
responsible for reviving him.

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:56.120
That’s why...

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.080
I’m gonna bring Orpheus down!

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:03.890
If he’s a monster who has conquered death,

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:05.710
I’ll seal him inside of myself!

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:08.840
I won’t let him outta my body!

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:12.380
You’d go to such lengths
to stand in our way...

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.220
To hamper the ideal Orpheus and I share!

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:17.020
I won’t let this end the way he wants!

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:20.880
Rook, I swear that I will save you!

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.450
Then give it your best shot.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.110
Follow me!

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:30.790
It looks like they both made
it through the first gates,

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:34.370
but the second gates won’t be so easy.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:38.010
The second gates are
isolated from each other.

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:40.600
Each gate has its own route.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:45.000
Kaito and Rook only have one possible route.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:49.480
This is a rather difficult puzzle.

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:55.990
He has solved an impossible puzzle and
rescued Master Rook once before!

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.140
I’m sure he can do it again!

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:07.650
I’m nowhere near close to the
second gate’s entrance!

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:15.880
As long as you fight for
a simultaneous entry,

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:18.410
I will always have the upper hand!

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:24.390
I simply have to worry about passing
through the gate before you.

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:25.660
It’s simple!

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:31.310
That’s it! I see my
route to the second gate!

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:36.850
Did he get the jump on me?!

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.680
That’s a waste of time.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:43.540
Mark my word!

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.310
There is no way you will defeat me.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:49.190
What makes you so sure?

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:53.450
Because... I know what the future holds.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:56.340
You’re the one who will
lose this puzzle battle.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:59.970
I know because that’s what
Orpheus saw in the future.

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:01.340
What?!

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:03.460
His premonitions are absolute.

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:08.090
No one can escape the fate
that he has foreseen!

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.460
Don’t give me that!

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:15.440
I won’t let Orpheus decide my future!

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:18.600
I’ll change my fate as
many times as it takes!

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:23.230
Rook, every time it comes down to it...

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.910
I WILL save you!

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.870
What?! Impossible!

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:41.590
At this rate, he’ll be
able to save Master Rook!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.000
No one can change the future seen by Orpheus!

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:52.000
Sweet! Now zoom on through!

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:53.380
That’s impossible!

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:58.810
Boo-yah!

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:05.140
Whatcha think? There's
no puzzle I can't solve!

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:08.700
If this keeps up, Kaito will win...

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:11.450
He can’t...! That can’t be right!

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:14.370
After all, Orpheus clearly
said that I would...

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:19.250
I see... A future where Kaito loses...

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:23.160
Is that what he meant?
Orpheus, that was mean...

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:28.570
Now if I can just match our timing so Rook

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:31.540
and I escape from this
puzzle at the same time...!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:35.800
Rook?

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:37.300
Hey!

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:39.730
Not good! At this rate...!

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:42.610
I won’t let you!

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:44.870
I’m not gonna let you
pull that stunt on me!

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:55.690
Perfect!

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.200
So it’s come to that...

00:18:58.750 --> 00:18:59.840
Master Rook!

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.700
Now we’ll both make it out!

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:11.040
Hey, Rook?

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.890
Kaito, you’ve lost this puzzle.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.690
Dude, what’re you talkin’ about?!

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:23.220
The tracks merge into one on
the way to the final gate.

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:24.470
They what...?

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:27.660
And there is only one gate.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:32.860
Then that means... only one
of us can pass through!

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:35.230
Yeah. And that person will be...

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:38.080
you, Kaito.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.620
Sure enough, you’re incredible, Kaito!

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:57.880
At last, I will become
“eternal” within you!

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:25.460
ROOK!

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:30.080
It has ended just as I foresaw.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:34.120
Kaito Daimon, I thought
you were a fascinating

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.090
individual capable of swaying the future,

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:37.600
but apparently I overestimated you.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:41.810
Despite rejecting the path
to becoming a Phi-Brain,

00:20:41.810 --> 00:20:45.190
Rook more than adequately
fulfilled his role as a pawn.

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:47.950
As for Kaito Daimon!

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:51.280
Your feelings for Rook will serve as fuel,

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:55.650
allowing you to grow ever closer
to becoming a Phi-Brain.

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:12.830
I believed in you!

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:16.180
I TRUSTED you! And yet you let him...

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:20.090
Master Rook...

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:24.560
Rook entrusted me with the future.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:43.230
You must...

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:49.450
You must defeat Orpheus... for Master Rook!

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:51.710
Count on it.

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:57.720
I swear I’ll take Orpheus down!

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:01.960
It’s time! At long last,
the time has come to select

00:22:02.390 --> 00:22:06.980
who is capable of serving as my
vessel from amongst these four.

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:22.580
Orpheus, you don’t get it.

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:27.450
It’s too much for Kaito and his friends!

00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:05.700
Hey, Kaito?

00:24:06.350 --> 00:24:10.310
We never would have grown to love
puzzles so much if not for you.

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:15.100
Well, at least your puzzle-fanaticism
kept me from gettin’ bored!

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:17.320
You’re not very honest with yourself.

00:24:17.320 --> 00:24:18.240
Shut it!

00:24:18.570 --> 00:24:21.230
Next time, “So, You
Shouldn’t Hesitate.”

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:27.980
So, You Shouldn’t Hesitate

00:24:21.870 --> 00:24:23.910
It’s time. I’m going on ahead.

00:24:23.910 --> 00:24:25.650
Bye, Kaito!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin
Art: Akeru Otsuki
